  "notes": "Drawn from 777Fs (G-DHMC 2026, D-AALO 2025, N773CK 2026). The DHL logo is a wordmark (drawn as titles; the speed lines as areas). The same scheme is worn by DHL's own airlines (EAT Leipzig, DHL Air UK, AeroLogic, Air Hong Kong, DHL Aero Expreso, DHL International Aviation ME) and by contractors' DHL-painted aircraft (Kalitta, ABX, ATI, Polar, Atlas, Southern...). The 757s, 767s, A300s and A330s wear it the same way; small operator titles ('Operated by Kalitta Air', 'AeroLogic') sit by the forward door. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on the 777F (G-DHMC 2026-03-01, N773CK 2026-06-12, D-AALO 2025-2026; every open photo is from below): the fuselage DHL had been drawn from just above the middle to the crown; on the photos its top is level with the forward door's top and its foot just under the lowest speed line before the D, with clear yellow above it, so it now runs y -0.27 to 0.33 (cap 0.6, from ~1.1). The speed lines after the L sit at the letters' foot, a little lower than those before the D (they had been drawn higher). The red belly's edge is a curve (smooth). The fin title reads 0.25-0.38 of the fin on G-DHMC but 0.33-0.42 on N773CK: left as drawn.",
  "history": "Replaces Skyarium v1's approximate standard (a few colors from memory). The yellow and red scheme came with Deutsche Post's 2002–2003 rebrand of DHL, replacing the white aircraft with red 'DHL' titles."
}
